>> title: Hoppin' John
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: beans, rice, southern, pork, stovetop
>> counters: Meat and Three, One Pot
>> aka: hopping john, peas and rice, black-eyed peas and rice
>> servings: 6
>> time: 1 hr 45 min
>> slack: unforgiving — the peas get their fifty minutes before the rice goes near them, or they stay hard in a pot that cannot cook on without turning to paste
>> step.1: render
>> step.2: sweat 8 min
>> step.3: simmer covered 50 min
>> step.4: cook covered 20 min
>> step.5: finish

Render @bacon{4%slices}(chopped) in a #Dutch oven{} until crisp.

Sweat @&(~1)bacon{} with @yellow onion{1%large}, @celery{2%ribs}, and @garlic{3%cloves} for ~{8%min}.

Simmer @&(~1)base{} covered for ~{50%min} with @dried black-eyed peas{1 1/2%cups}(280 g; soaked overnight), @chicken stock{5%cups}(1.2 L), @bay leaf{1}, and @cayenne{1/4%tsp}.

Cook @&(~1)peas{} covered for ~{20%min} with @long-grain white rice{1%cup}(200 g) and @kosher salt{2%tsp}.

Finish @&(~1)hoppin' john{} with @cider vinegar{1%Tbs} and @scallions{3}(sliced).
